## Governance Posture

AI Agents may analyze, classify, recommend, and produce proposals when those capabilities are applicable to the project. They MUST NOT infer Authority from Capability, self-grant Authority, or treat their own Proposal as an AuthorizedDecision.

{{if .Project.AI.ConsequentialExecution}}Consequential AI execution is declared in scope and must be bounded by applicable Authority, Policy, State, Risk, and Verification controls before effects occur.{{else}}Consequential AI execution is not declared in scope. Generated project guidance therefore treats AI behavior as advisory by default.{{end}}

## Control Status

See `.aof/config.yaml` for the explicit project control matrix. `Deferred` and `Unsupported` are visible gaps and MUST NOT be interpreted as satisfied. `NotApplicable` MUST reflect true non-applicability.
